## Codebook `fr_gr.shp`

Overview of variables:

id: municipal ID
GISCO_I: GISCO Municipality Identifier
CNTR_CODE_: FR if France, NA if Germany
LAU_ID: Local Administrative Area (EU-standard) municipality ID
LAU_NAM: Name of municipality
POP_201: Population in 2019
POP_DEN: Population density in 2019
AREA_KM: Area of municipality (sq. km.)
YEAR: Year at which municipality is registered in database (not important)
FID_x: France Municipal ID (don't use)
NAME_LA, NUTS_NA: Name of NUTS_3 area in which municipality falls (France only)
CNTR_CODE: FR if France, DE if Germany
nuts_3: NUTS-3 code of NUTS-3 area in which municipality falls
LVL_CO: Discard
nuts_2: NUTS-2 code of NUTS-2 area in which municipality falls
mn_ds__: minimum distance to Roman Road
tretmnt: 1 if Roman Road stretches through municipality, 0 if not but Roman Road stretches to neighbour municipality, NA otherwise

URBN_TY, COAST_T: coastal and urban scores from 1-3 for France